    <exercise number="5" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>How do you graph a piecewise function?</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>Graph each formula of the piecewise function over its corresponding domain. Use the same scale for the $$x x$$ -axis and $$y y$$ -axis for each graph. Indicate inclusive endpoints with a solid circle and exclusive endpoints with an open circle. Use an arrow to indicate $$-\infty -\infty$$ or $$\infty . \infty .$$ Combine the graphs to find the graph of the piecewise function.</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
